WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.093
Do not automate a broken process.

00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:03.488
Fix the path first.

00:00:03.488 --> 00:00:05.929
This lesson is about simple automations later.

00:00:05.929 --> 00:00:07.673
Don't automate a broken process.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.114
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:13.602
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:18.833
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.669
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:22.669 --> 00:00:27.552
Stay practical: list what not to automate yet before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.872 --> 00:00:31.805
Automations come later: after you have repeated the steps by hand.

00:00:31.805 --> 00:00:35.022
Remember the objective: list what not to automate yet.

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:38.955
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:43.245
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.245 --> 00:00:47.177
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:51.467
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.970
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.400
Feedback beats guessing alone.

